1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,911
Sending a Private repository URL alone does not give your
instructor access.

2
00:00:06,911 --> 00:00:12,822
In your repository Settings, choose Collaborators and Add
people.

3
00:00:12,822 --> 00:00:21,370
Check the full course instructor username, select the match,
and confirm the final Add button.

4
00:00:21,370 --> 00:00:29,373
Pending means your invitation was sent, while instructor
access still awaits acceptance.

5
00:00:29,373 --> 00:00:32,738
Do not repeat an accepted invitation.

6
00:00:32,738 --> 00:00:34,920
Pause to check the list.

7
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:37,920
Pause here and check your own screen.

8
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:44,840
Save all required files, then return to Code at the root of
your repository.

9
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:52,853
At the upper right of the file list, click the clock icon
and the number beside Commits.

10
00:00:52,853 --> 00:00:56,404
A narrow screen may show only the icon.

11
00:00:56,404 --> 00:01:00,046
This is not the global menu or Insights.

12
00:01:00,046 --> 00:01:02,960
Pause and open your own history.

13
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:05,960
Pause here and check your own screen.

14
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:11,872
Click the newest message after all your required files were
saved.

15
00:01:11,872 --> 00:01:18,502
The address contains slash commit slash followed by the
commit identifier.

16
00:01:18,502 --> 00:01:22,175
Check the author, time, and save message.

17
00:01:22,175 --> 00:01:28,983
The Copy SHA button copies only the identifier, not the full
submission URL.

18
00:01:28,983 --> 00:01:31,760
Pause and open the commit page.

19
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:34,760
Pause here and check your own screen.

20
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:37,620
A commit page mainly shows changes.

21
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:44,647
Use Browse files at the upper right to inspect the complete
file list at that version.

22
00:01:44,647 --> 00:01:50,040
Check the required README and artifacts in the chosen week
folder.

23
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:55,841
If a file is missing, add and save it, then use the newer
final commit.

24
00:01:55,841 --> 00:01:59,600
Return to the commit page to copy its address.

25
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,600
Pause here and check your own screen.

26
00:02:02,600 --> 00:02:05,659
Return to the checked commit page.

27
00:02:05,659 --> 00:02:13,486
On Windows, use Control L to select the address bar and
Control C to copy the full URL.

28
00:02:13,486 --> 00:02:21,583
Open the weekly form from your course page, check the
account, week, and URL, then submit.

29
00:02:21,583 --> 00:02:24,102
Check the form confirmation.

30
00:02:24,102 --> 00:02:28,600
Saving on GitHub alone has not submitted the form.

31
00:02:28,600 --> 00:02:31,600
Pause here and check your own screen.

32
00:02:31,600 --> 00:02:34,137
Check four things separately.

33
00:02:34,137 --> 00:02:36,936
Do you own a Private repository?

34
00:02:36,936 --> 00:02:39,560
Can you reopen the saved text?

35
00:02:39,560 --> 00:02:42,710
Is the instructor invitation listed?

36
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:45,247
Did the form confirm receipt?

37
00:02:45,247 --> 00:02:52,507
The Verified badge on a commit is not instructor review or
submission confirmation.

38
00:02:52,507 --> 00:02:56,444
Tell your instructor which check stopped you.

39
00:02:56,444 --> 00:03:01,080
These checks describe your operation, not your grade.

40
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:04,080
Pause here and check your own screen.
